From 9e7b9c319506b20a216696e922ae8afe3cf52ea7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Zila <john@jzila.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Jan 2026 20:46:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(canopy): pass user prompt to agents with instruction
 precedence
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User prompt instructions passed via --prompt flag are now included in
the agent prompt with clear precedence markers. Previously, the prompt
was only used for filtering tasks but agents never saw the user's
instructions.

The prompt is now structured as:
1. User Instructions (marked PRIORITY) - at the top
2. Dependency context - from upstream tasks
3. Task title and description - from bead
4. IMPORTANT reminder - reiterating user boundaries

This ensures agents follow user scope/boundaries (e.g., "stop before
running tests") rather than following bead descriptions blindly.

